    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d990">

                <pb facs="1152" n="956" xml:id="pg956"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Department of the Army Files: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 990<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Military Attaché in Sweden</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Kessler</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the War
                        Department</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d990-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-24">24 July 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>667. For ComGenAir MilID Washington D. C.</p>
                <p>Russian Delegation here conducted survey of interned German aircraft presumably
                    those coining here from German Soviet front. Russians propose to fly these out
                    shortly as war booty. Their plans have been publicized in newspapers. See my 591
                    of 26 June and your 28542 of 7 July.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d990-f2"/> Newspapers
                    also carried item that neither UK or US have made request concerning
                    remainder.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kessler</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d990-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d990-f1-content">
                <p>Received by the United States Delegation to the Berlin Conference on July 25 as a
                    retransmission from the War Department.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d990-f2" n="2" xml:id="d990-f2-content">
                <p>Neither printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
